@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `br-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `br-lindb-conflict-of-laws`

-- Readings of the text that this encoding REJECTS, written as the expectation each reading would produce.
-- EVERY assertion in this file is meant to fail: it fails because the encoding gives the other answer. That is the point of the file.
-- check.sh counts them: expected_failed for this file is 8, and encoding.json says the same under expected_red.
-- A refusal cannot go here, because a plain #ASSERT on an expression that refuses is "refused", which turns the whole run red;
-- so only rejected readings that would give a different VALUE are listed.

§ `Art. 1 caput: "quarenta e cinco dias depois de oficialmente publicada"`

-- Rejected: the publication day is itself the first of the 45 days, so the law binds 44 days after it. The text says "depois de",
-- after the publication, and does not count the publication day as one of the days.
#ASSERT `the day` 45 `days after` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 23

-- Rejected: 45 full days must pass after the publication day, so the law binds on the 46th day.
#ASSERT `the day` 45 `days after` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 25

§ `Art. 1 par. 1: "três meses depois"`

-- Rejected: a month is thirty days, so three months is ninety days. The text names no length for a month and says nothing about thirty days;
-- the encoding reads a month as a calendar month with the same day number.
#ASSERT `the day` 3 `months after` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 8

§ `Art. 7 par. 6: "depois de 1 (um) ano da data da sentença"`

-- Rejected: a year is 365 days, so one year after 1 March 2023 is 29 February 2024 (there is a leap day in between).
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `years after` (YMD 2023 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29

-- Rejected: two years are 730 days, so two years after 28 February 2024 is 27 February 2026.
#ASSERT `the day` 2 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 27

§ `Art. 17: "a soberania nacional, a ordem pública e os bons costumes"`

-- Rejected: all three must be offended together. The encoding reads the list as three separate grounds, any one of which denies efficacy.
#ASSERT NOT `art. 17 denies the foreign law, act, judgment or declaration of will efficacy in Brazil` TRUE FALSE FALSE

§ `Art. 11 par. 2 and par. 3`

-- Rejected: par. 2 prevails, so a foreign government may not acquire even a building needed for its diplomatic seat. Par. 3 would then
-- say nothing. The encoding tries par. 3 first.
#ASSERT NOT `a foreign government or its organisation may acquire the property in Brazil` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE

§ `Art. 10 par. 1: "sempre que não lhes seja mais favorável a lei pessoal do de cujus"`

-- Rejected: Brazilian law governs the succession of a foreigner's assets in Brazil whenever a Brazilian spouse or child benefits, even where the
-- deceased's personal law is more favourable to them. The text takes the case where the personal law is more favourable out.
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs a succession` "Italy" TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS "Brazil"
